---
import ModuleLayout from '../../../../layouts/ModuleLayout.astro';
---
<ModuleLayout title="Cardiac" moduleId="cardiac" icon="❤️" description="Chest pain differentials, ACS, heart failure, arrhythmias, hypertension, and ECG basics" activeTab="assessment">
  <div class="content-prose">
    <h2>Cardiac History</h2>
    <div class="assessment-grid">
      <div class="assessment-card">
        <div class="card-header"><div class="icon-circle">❓</div><h4>Chest Pain — Key Questions</h4></div>
        <ul>
          <li>Onset — sudden or gradual? What were you doing?</li>
          <li>Location — central, left-sided, right-sided? Retrosternal?</li>
          <li>Radiation — to jaw, left arm, shoulder, back, epigastrium?</li>
          <li>Character — pressure, tightness, squeezing, burning, sharp, tearing?</li>
          <li>Severity — 0–10 pain scale</li>
          <li>Duration — seconds, minutes, hours, constant?</li>
          <li>Relieving factors — GTN, rest, antacids, position, analgesia?</li>
          <li>Aggravating factors — exertion, inspiration, palpation, eating?</li>
          <li>Associated: dyspnoea, diaphoresis, nausea, syncope, palpitations?</li>
          <li>Previous identical episodes?</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="assessment-card">
        <div class="card-header"><div class="icon-circle">📋</div><h4>Cardiac Risk Factors</h4></div>
        <ul>
          <li>Age and sex (male &gt;45, female &gt;55 or post-menopausal)</li>
          <li>Known IHD, previous MI, PCI, CABG</li>
          <li>Hypertension — diagnosed and treatment</li>
          <li>Hyperlipidaemia — LDL, total cholesterol</li>
          <li>Diabetes — type, duration, glycaemic control</li>
          <li>Smoking — pack-year history, current status</li>
          <li>Family history — first-degree relative, premature CAD &lt;55M/65F</li>
          <li>Obesity and physical inactivity</li>
          <li>Chronic kidney disease</li>
          <li>Atrial fibrillation or other arrhythmia</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="assessment-card">
        <div class="card-header"><div class="icon-circle">💧</div><h4>Heart Failure History</h4></div>
        <ul>
          <li>Dyspnoea — at rest, on exertion, NYHA class?</li>
          <li>Orthopnoea — how many pillows?</li>
          <li>Paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnoea</li>
          <li>Ankle and leg oedema — onset, extent, pitting?</li>
          <li>Exercise tolerance — how far can you walk?</li>
          <li>Weight gain — recent rapid increase (fluid)?</li>
          <li>Fatigue and reduced effort tolerance</li>
          <li>Nocturia (increased renal perfusion when supine)</li>
          <li>Known echo findings — EF, valvular disease</li>
          <li>Current medications and compliance</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="assessment-card">
        <div class="card-header"><div class="icon-circle">〰️</div><h4>Palpitations and Arrhythmia</h4></div>
        <ul>
          <li>Onset — sudden or gradual? What triggers?</li>
          <li>Character — fast, slow, irregular, missed beats?</li>
          <li>Duration — seconds to minutes or sustained?</li>
          <li>Associated: dyspnoea, chest pain, presyncope, syncope?</li>
          <li>Termination — spontaneous, Valsalva, position?</li>
          <li>Caffeine, alcohol, exercise relationship</li>
          <li>Thyroid disease, anaemia, electrolyte disturbance</li>
          <li>Previous AF or arrhythmia diagnosis</li>
          <li>Current anticoagulation or antiarrhythmic medications</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Cardiovascular Examination</h2>
    <div class="assessment-grid">
      <div class="assessment-card">
        <div class="card-header"><div class="icon-circle">🔍</div><h4>General and Vital Signs</h4></div>
        <ul>
          <li>Appearance — distress, diaphoresis, pallor, cyanosis</li>
          <li>BP — both arms (dissection screen), lying and standing</li>
          <li>HR — rate, rhythm, character</li>
          <li>RR — tachypnoea suggests decompensation</li>
          <li>SpO2 — on air and with supplemental oxygen</li>
          <li>Temperature — fever may indicate infective endocarditis</li>
          <li>BMI and waist circumference</li>
          <li>12-lead ECG — perform early in all chest pain</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="assessment-card">
        <div class="card-header"><div class="icon-circle">👁️</div><h4>Peripheral Signs</h4></div>
        <ul>
          <li>Hands — clubbing, splinter haemorrhages, peripheral cyanosis</li>
          <li>Eyes — xanthelasma, corneal arcus, anaemia, Roth spots</li>
          <li>Face — malar flush (mitral stenosis)</li>
          <li>Neck — JVP height and waveform, carotid bruits</li>
          <li>Legs — peripheral oedema (pitting, extent), varicosities</li>
          <li>Calves — DVT signs (PE risk)</li>
          <li>Peripheral pulses — femoral, popliteal, pedal</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="assessment-card">
        <div class="card-header"><div class="icon-circle">🫀</div><h4>Precordial Examination</h4></div>
        <ul>
          <li>Inspection — visible pulsations, scars (sternotomy, pacemaker)</li>
          <li>Palpation — apex beat location and character</li>
          <li>Palpation — heaves and thrills</li>
          <li>Auscultation — S1 and S2 character and splitting</li>
          <li>Added sounds — S3 (HF), S4 (stiff ventricle), clicks</li>
          <li>Murmurs — timing, location, radiation, character, grade</li>
          <li>Lung bases — bilateral crackles suggest pulmonary oedema</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="assessment-card">
        <div class="card-header"><div class="icon-circle">📊</div><h4>Investigations to Order</h4></div>
        <ul>
          <li>12-lead ECG — always first in chest pain or palpitations</li>
          <li>High sensitivity troponin — 0h and 2h (or 0h and 3h)</li>
          <li>FBE — anaemia, infection</li>
          <li>EUC — renal function, electrolytes</li>
          <li>BGL and HbA1c</li>
          <li>Fasting lipids — total, LDL, HDL, TG</li>
          <li>TFTs — hyperthyroidism causes AF and palpitations</li>
          <li>BNP or NT-proBNP — heart failure diagnosis and monitoring</li>
          <li>CXR — cardiomegaly, pulmonary oedema, pleural effusion</li>
          <li>Echo — if new murmur, HF suspected, or post-ACS</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Risk Scoring Tools</h2>
    <div class="assessment-grid">
      <div class="assessment-card">
        <div class="card-header"><div class="icon-circle">🎯</div><h4>HEART Score (Chest Pain)</h4></div>
        <ul>
          <li>H — History: highly suspicious (2), moderately (1), slightly (0)</li>
          <li>E — ECG: LBBB/ST changes (2), non-specific (1), normal (0)</li>
          <li>A — Age: ≥65 (2), 45–64 (1), &lt;45 (0)</li>
          <li>R — Risk factors: ≥3 or atherosclerosis (2), 1–2 (1), none (0)</li>
          <li>T — Troponin: &gt;3x normal (2), 1–3x (1), normal (0)</li>
          <li>Score 0–3: low risk (1.7% MACE) — consider discharge</li>
          <li>Score 4–6: moderate risk — observe, serial troponins</li>
          <li>Score 7–10: high risk — early invasive strategy</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="assessment-card">
        <div class="card-header"><div class="icon-circle">🩸</div><h4>NYHA Functional Class (Heart Failure)</h4></div>
        <ul>
          <li>Class I — No symptoms with ordinary activity</li>
          <li>Class II — Slight limitation, comfortable at rest, symptoms with moderate exertion</li>
          <li>Class III — Marked limitation, comfortable at rest, symptoms with minimal exertion</li>
          <li>Class IV — Symptoms at rest, inability to carry on any activity</li>
          <li>Used to guide therapy titration and referral</li>
          <li>NYHA III–IV → urgent cardiology referral</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</ModuleLayout>
